<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Talatal Ghar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Talatal Ghar is a royal palace of the Ahom kingdom at Rangpur, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivasagar">Sivasagar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>. Begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudra-singha">Rudra Singha</a> in the early eighteenth century and enlarged by later kings, notably Rajeswar Singha, it is the largest Ahom monument: a multi-storeyed brick building whose upper part is known as the Kareng Ghar, with lower levels used for stores and military quarters.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/talatal-ghar.jpg" alt="Talatal Ghar" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joli Rumi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Talatal_Ghar_in_Sivasagar,_Assam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
